doc episodes 6 Episode 1: "Standards" — T lets rip at half-time.
Cold open: The episode opens in the tunnel after the 1-1 draw with Coventry City (Saka) in the Premier League.
Half-time: Cameras catch T slamming the tactics board in the dressing room. The players sit in silence; nobody looks up.
Training ground: A rare clean bill of health for the squad. Bukayo Saka leads the scoring charts with 1 this season.
Closing: The season has barely started. Next up: Brentford (Premier League) on 29 Aug. The narrator closes the episode: "In this building, there is no such thing as a quiet week." 
QUOTES T (Manager): A point. A point! We had them there and we let them off. Not again.
Dylan Pearce (Assistant manager): When he goes like that, you just let it land. Ten minutes later he's hugging everyone.
Mason Okoro (Academy player): My mum's watching this, so I'm on my best behaviour.
Narrator (Series voice-over): Every club tells itself a story. This one is still deciding how it ends.
